{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1548286-a-nation-divided","id":1548286,"title":"A Nation Divided","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-02-07T02:45:32-08:00","id":1548286,"title":"A Nation Divided","content":"So one aspect of WtE (and to a lesser extent by nights studieos verson of WtA) that I found really fascinating is the fact that the garou nation is split into two factions (the Eastern and Western Concordat) due to the death of it's king and subsequent political turmoil that follows. While the resulting factions are technically working toward the same goals as each other (protecting Gaia, killing banes, ect) but the means they want to achieve them (direct action for the west cons vs east cons more subtle means) is slightly different between said factions which leads to tensions between the faction but not open conflict. Resulting in something that could be described as a Civil Cold War.<br /> <br /> I also found a post on Tumblr that outline a similar scenario from above:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://pardy-dardy.tumblr.com/post/772253463963942912/btwod-the-garou-nation-we-all-saw-it-coming-pt\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://64.media.tumblr.com/c4914899d74a348f633eac51afee849a/eeca6564b939842c-06/s128x128u_c1/a1008a4dd780c6492c425b395914d85a4c4b5dd4.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://pardy-dardy.tumblr.com/post/772253463963942912/btwod-the-garou-nation-we-all-saw-it-coming-pt\" target=\"_blank\"> BtWoD: The Garou Nation; We All Saw It Coming Pt. 1 </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://pardy-dardy.tumblr.com/post/772253463963942912/btwod-the-garou-nation-we-all-saw-it-coming-pt\" target=\"_blank\"> https://pardy-dardy.tumblr.com/post/772253463963942912/btwod-the-garou-nation-we-all-saw-it-coming-pt </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> so. in the BtWoD continuity, the Garou Nation fell sometime in the early 2000s thanks to internal conflict, dissatisfaction with leadership, the death of Jonas Albrecht, and the ever-increasing... </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> mainly the death of king Albrecht caused political tensions between the tribes to flare up causing the garou nation to split. Only instead of the tribes reorganizing into two alliances like above, this version of the garou nation of this timeline are for a lack of a better word Balkanized where all the tribes are spilt and reorganized along National and cultural lines and going they separate ways.<br /> <br /> I wonder what you guys would think about a concept of a divided garou nation, what stores would you like to tell with that setup and what other scenario that involves splitting the nation would look like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 02-07-2025, 08:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-07T14:46:09-08:00","id":1548310,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s interesting to wonder if the division of the Garou nation into competing blocs (The By Night studios status quo) might have been a precondition for the shattered nation of the Fifth Edition - a depressing thought, but not implausible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-07T23:05:42-08:00","id":1548320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1548286-a-nation-divided?p=1548310#post1548310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It\u2019s interesting to wonder if the division of the Garou nation into competing blocs (The By Night studios status quo) might have been a precondition for the shattered nation of the Fifth Edition - a depressing thought, but not implausible.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To be fair I suspect the nation falling apart in W5 is more of a decision influenced by the higher up at paradox rather than anything to do with BNS. And besides the garou nation falling apart could make for a compelling setting.<br /> <br /> Take the setting laid out in the tumblr post as an example. the tribes instead just laying down and giving up like what's implied in W5 they actually either reorganized into a diffrent alliances basically creating a series of localized mini garou nations:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Coyote\u2019s Council</i><br /> This one\u2019s a fun one. After the Garou Nation crumbled, Patron Spirit Coyote went out recruiting from all of the Garou in North America who had native blood in them. Most of them were frmr. Ghost Council + mixed Bone Gnawers, but who knows how many other ex-Tribes were mixed in. Nowadays, they take orders from Patron Coyote, and they\u2019re publicly working with the Nuwisha to the end of their shared master.<br /> <br /> Has this made them more fun? Yes and no. They\u2019re <i>still </i>Garou, and we all know how they can get when they\u2019re the butt of a joke. But a bunch of them have embraced their inner coyote, and have turned into a well-oiled guerilla force in the process. Some of the reports coming out of the US\u2019 interior sound like the plot to a rejected Tom &amp; Jerry episode, if I\u2019m being honest.<br /> <br /> Strangely, they can\u2019t be found outside of the North American continent. With the efficacy they\u2019re showing, you\u2019d think that Patron Coyote would want to start stretching his paws. But, nope. As of the publishing of this report, the only other place Coyote\u2019s Council is found is in the Umbra, but that much should be obvious.<br /> <br /> And, of course, they\u2019re cagey as hell when it comes to their plans. Don\u2019t trust a damn thing they\u2019re feeding you unless you\u2019ve got a prior arrangement, or have them under a Geas or something.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Fangs of the High North</i><br /> Before this section begins, a preface; Canada is off-limits. The Fangs of the High North are in the process of skirmishing with colonizing Garou (in addition to their usual activities of destroying Pentex infrastructure where they can), and the place is dangerous to the Corax. We\u2019ve been told on multiple occasions that if we\u2019re not there to actively help, we\u2019re to stay the fuck away. While I\u2019m not an advisor, I can say for certain that it scared the shit out of me, and that I can\u2019t say I\u2019d encourage anyone else to head there, not even for migratory purposes.<br /> <br /> So, yeah! The Fangs are another neo-Tribe native to North America, and are primarily made up of frmr. Gale Stalkers, Red Talons, and sympathetic Get of Fenris. Now that the Nation is out of their way, they\u2019ve been looking to take back their land by force. Can\u2019t say I blame them. They\u2019ve been on the warpath ever since, and considering how many other native Fera are joining the effort, I\u2019m of the opinion that there\u2019s a good chance they\u2019ll give those bastards the boot.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s just hope that none of the occupiers get desperate enough to turn to Malfeas for help. As of the time of publishing, there\u2019ve been no reports of unusual Wyrmtaint coming from some of our American kin, so keep your feathers crossed! </div> </div> </div>Or just one tribe consolidate they resources so they can operate as an independent tribe without the support of the fallen nation:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Get of Fenris</i><br /> Okay. The Get has (to nobody\u2019s surprise) become the dominant Garou Tribe in the European Continent, has made significant progress in recruiting pissed off Americans from the North and South continents, and has found incredible success in changing literally nothing about their viking/berserker philosophy. In fact, the crumbling of the Garou Nation was a GOOD THING for their leadership, as they now are unbound by any bureaucracy. We\u2019re all <i>very</i> familiar with these details by now.<br /> <br /> One thing I want to put to bed before you birdbrains start freaking out is this\u2014 THE GET ARE NOT NAZIS. The Get have a longstanding tradition (that HAS BEEN WELL CATALOGUED BY THE CORAX, LEARN TO VISIT THE LIBRARY) of forcing their cubs to shed all former ties to their human lives if they\u2019re born Homid, including any kind of racist beliefs they might hold. ANY Get found participating in upholding any form of hierarchy OTHER than \u201cmight makes right\u201d is immediately liable to being ganked by their peers until the racism leaves their bodies. I\u2019<i>ve literally seen it happen.</i> And yeah, there was a faction of them back in WW2, but <i>we all had some dead branches to trim from our kin back then.</i><br /> <br /> Does it excuse their behavior? Abso-fucking-lutely not. But if you want to start pointing fingers at <i>real</i> Nazis, we\u2019ve got dossiers your Pack can to be assigned to. Put your activism to <i>real</i> work, kids </div> </div> </div>And that not to mention that the restively simple premise of the garou nation splitting into two blocs offers plenty of opportunities for authors and ST's present instances of political intrigue between the tribes.<br /> <br /> Like take the Glass Walkers in WtE as an example. They're one of the tribes initially supported the Eastern Concordat during it's formation, but they shifted allegiance to the Western Concordat partly due to the fact that the Eastern Concordat is welling to work with the hearthbound, (a radical pro kinfolk activist group turned tribe who depending on the garou are people fighting for the to save the nation from it's self or terrorists who wants to cause rifts in the tribes) in addition to they spotty history with kinfolks. Thoug they sill try to maintain contact with the Eastern Concordat to act as bridge between the two blocs, despite the obvious bad blood between them.<br /> <br /> Also a consequence of the Glass Walkers joining the Western Concordat is the Red Talons splitting off from the alliance, becoming an independent tribe.<br /> <br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://imgur.com/343GRnB.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://imgur.com/343GRnB.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://imgur.com/343GRnB.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> Though there's a in-unverse conspiracy theory that the Shadow Lords (effectively the founding tribe of Eastcon) suggested the Glass Walkers to join the Western Concordat to counteract the extremist influence the Red Talons has on the bloc and them leaving is a favorable outcome for the Shadow Lords.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mundusartis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540073-wte-final-layout-preview?p=1542399#post1542399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When the Nation split, they initially joined the Western Concordat. When the Glass Walkers quit the eastern concordat and joined the westcons it so thoroughly alienated the Red Talons that they dropped what tenuous affiliations they once had altogether. This outcome is one that's driven mixed opinions between tribes. On one hand, they are losing potential allies.<b> On the other hand, with the Red Talons out of the Western Concordat, the faction is a lot less likely to trend towards extremism, leading some to think the Glass Walkers scoffing at the Eastcons' acceptance of the Hearthbound and joining the Westcons may have been a political maneuver catalyzed by the Shadow Lords to shift the Overton Window away from extremism</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-10T14:36:22-08:00","id":1548376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1548286-a-nation-divided?p=1548320#post1548320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also a consequence of the Glass Walkers joining the Western Concordat is the Red Talons splitting off from the alliance, becoming an independent tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Expanding on the red talions going isolationist, while before the apcoypise they could and indeed have survive independently of the garou nation, assuming they maintain they Carens, unfortunately the Apocalypse wiped out most of carens with only 13 surviving and the fallout of the Apocalypse rendered the classic rituals for making more carens as bane bait.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mundusartis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540073-wte-final-layout-preview?p=1542859#post1542859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The old Caern-building rites have effectively become bane-summoning rites from start to finish, making the creation of new caerns (called Great Caerns in this setting) more or less impossible. A shard caern is so-named after its heart, which is little more than a spiritual sliver taken from the heart of one of the 13 remaining Great Caerns. They are weaker and far more vulnerable to attack but retain the same abilities and powers reflecting the Great Caern that provided the shard.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which is really Unfortunate, for the Red Talons since the preview material I've read indicate they don't own any of the 13 carens meaning if the Red Talons want to survive long term they have to negotiate with the other tribes for access to one of the surviving 13 Caern or access to a shard seed (an artifact that's nesscary for creating new caerns in the post Apocalypse) else the tribe would face a slow death. And from what I've know Negotiations isn't the Red Talions Strong suite...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 02-10-2025, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}